# Workstation

Roles are ways of thinking. They are not tied to a second computer.

```text
Owner
  → ChatGPT (Mac): control, Gate Review, architecture judgment, task split, instruct Grok Bot, retro
  → Mac Cursor: Design Station. @ one of Product Manager, UX Architect, UI Designer, Backend Architect
  → Mac Grok Bot: primary engineer. code, tests, fixes, git, test-environment deploy
  → GitHub: the only remote source of truth
  → 51.81.146.19: later Human Acceptance Environment
```

Another Cursor account is capacity backup for the same Mac workspace, not another workstation.

Main line: Think → See → Decide → Freeze → Build → Verify. All of it can happen on one Mac.

# Single writer

Only one agent holds the write mindset at a time. Others may read and recommend. They do not edit the same files in parallel.

Naming a role with `@` does not grant `edit`, `commit`, `push`, `deploy`, or `production_access`. Those stay separate and default to false.

`51.81.146.19` is a future acceptance host. Naming it does not authorize deployment, and no credentials belong in this repo. Adapters and deployment configuration still need a separate reviewed gate.
